BANKWISE DEMO BANK
ACCOUNT SERVICES GUIDE

1. INTRODUCTION

BankWise Demo Bank provides different types of bank accounts for personal and business banking needs. This document explains common account services, features, requirements, and general procedures.

This is a fictional/demo document created for the BankWise AI RAG project. It is not an official banking policy.

2. SAVINGS ACCOUNT

A savings account is generally used by individuals for saving money and performing everyday banking activities.

Common features include:
• Depositing and withdrawing money
• ATM/debit card access
• Internet and mobile banking
• UPI services
• Account statements
• Digital fund transfers

The exact features, interest rates, and charges depend on the account type and applicable bank policies.

3. CURRENT ACCOUNT

A current account is generally designed for customers who need frequent financial transactions, including businesses and organizations.

Common features may include:
• Frequent deposits and withdrawals
• Business transactions
• Digital banking services
• Fund transfers
• Account statements

Minimum balance requirements and service charges may vary depending on the account type.

4. ACCOUNT OPENING

A customer generally needs to provide identification and other information requested by the bank when opening an account.

Common requirements may include:
• Government-approved identity document
• Address information
• Photograph, where applicable
• Mobile number
• Email address, where applicable
• Other documents required by the bank

The exact requirements can vary according to the account type and applicable regulations.

5. MINIMUM BALANCE

Some bank accounts may require customers to maintain a minimum balance. Other account types may have different balance requirements.

Customers should check the current account terms and schedule of charges before opening an account.

6. ACCOUNT STATEMENT

An account statement provides information about transactions and account activity.

Customers may be able to obtain statements through:
• Internet banking
• Mobile banking
• ATM services
• Bank branch
• Other official banking channels

7. ACCOUNT BALANCE

Customers can check their available account balance through supported official channels such as mobile banking, internet banking, ATMs, or a bank branch.

Customers should use only official banking applications and websites when checking account information.

8. NOMINEE INFORMATION

A nominee is a person designated according to applicable banking procedures to receive or claim account-related benefits after the account holder's death.

Customers should contact their bank to understand the applicable nomination process and requirements.

9. UPDATING ACCOUNT INFORMATION

Customers may need to update information such as:
• Address
• Mobile number
• Email address
• KYC information
• Other customer details

Updates should be made only through official banking channels.

10. CLOSING A BANK ACCOUNT

A customer who wants to close an account should follow the bank's official account-closure procedure.

The customer may need to:
• Submit an account-closure request
• Provide required identification
• Clear applicable dues
• Return or deactivate relevant banking instruments where required
• Follow the bank's verification process

11. ACCOUNT SECURITY

Customers should protect their banking information.

Never share:
• OTP
• ATM PIN
• UPI PIN
• Internet banking password
• CVV
• Card credentials
• Other authentication information

The bank's official support channels should be used for account-related problems.

12. IMPORTANT NOTE

BankWise AI is an informational chatbot for the BankWise AI RAG project. It does not access real bank accounts, view customer balances, perform transactions, transfer money, approve loans, or modify account information.

For account-specific issues, customers should contact their actual bank through its official website, mobile application, helpline, or branch.

DISCLAIMER

Account features, charges, minimum balance requirements, documentation, eligibility, and procedures may vary between banks and may change over time. Always verify current information through the relevant bank's official channels.
